Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"

Hi TLS and PLANTS friends,

There was some feedback that id-rdna-trustAnchorID from
draft-ietf-plants-merkle-tree-certs would be useful in contexts outside of
MTC. This attribute was defined in MTC for CAs which are (by construction)
new enough to be directly named by trust anchor ID.

There's nothing special about MTC here. The same could apply to any
ecosystem where it makes sense to identify CAs this way. This means, at
least in the basic case, we have an easy way to configure relying parties,
even for non-MTC CAs.

I've uploaded a PR to start it off.
https://github.com/tlswg/tls-trust-anchor-ids/pull/133

The plan would be to land that PR, cut draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids-07,
then update draft-ietf-plants-merkle-tree-certs to just cite that text, and
finally cut draft-ietf-plants-merkle-tree-certs-08. This doesn't change the
wire format of either document, just moves some text around and gives
id-rdna-trustAnchorID
a clearer definition on its own. (There's already a separate extension for
denoting that a CA certificate is an MTC CA.)

We already have an early allocation, pointing to an MTC draft. Hopefully it
won't cause too much confusion if it gets repointed to a different RFC by
the end?

Funny how we only just removed the ASN.1 module from
draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids-05, :-)

David

--000000000000ad98ff065df9f15b
